{"id":"en-153","title":"How to Connect an External Blower to Laser","family":"x-series","topic":"guides","read_minutes":1,"source_url":"https://wiki.1laser.com/en/x-series/connect-external-blower-laser-machine","source_updated_at":"2026-01-29T04:16:23.707Z","body_html":"<div><h2 id=\"how-to-connect-an-external-blower\"> How to Connect an External Blower</h2><div>\n\n</div><p>\n  How to Connect External Blower explains how to safely connect an external air blower \n  to a laser machine for improved ventilation and cutting performance. \n  This guide covers preparation, required tools, and step-by-step installation \n  to ensure proper airflow and reliable operation.\n</p><div>\n\n</div><h2 id=\"h-1-preparation\"> 1. Preparation</h2><div>\n\n</div><h3 id=\"h-1-consumable-preparation\"> ① Consumable preparation</h3>\n<p>One Laser X model device ×1</p>\n<p>M2 hexagon wrench</p><div>\n\n</div><h3 id=\"h-2-debug-software\"> ② Debug software</h3>\n<p>None</p><div>\n\n</div><h2 id=\"h-2-operation-step\"> 2. Operation step</h2><div>\n\n</div><p>\n  ① Use an M2 hexagon wrench to loosen the six screws on the right side panel \n  and remove the side panel.\n</p><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/connect-external-blower-laser-machine/connect-external-blower-laser-machine_1.jpg\" alt=\"Removing right side panel of laser machine\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>② Press the blue air valve to draw out the built-in air.</p><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/connect-external-blower-laser-machine/connect-external-blower-laser-machine_2.jpg\" alt=\"Pressing blue air valve inside laser machine\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/connect-external-blower-laser-machine/connect-external-blower-laser-machine_3.jpg\" alt=\"Built-in air valve connection point\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>③ Insert the external air tube into the blue air valve nozzle.</p><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/connect-external-blower-laser-machine/connect-external-blower-laser-machine_4.jpg\" alt=\"Connecting external air tube to air valve\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>\n  ④ Insert the external air pipe into the air nozzle valve \n  and turn on the external air compressor.\n</p><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/connect-external-blower-laser-machine/connect-external-blower-laser-machine_5.jpg\" alt=\"External blower connected and air compressor running\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure>\n</div>","headings":[{"level":1,"id":"how-to-connect-an-external-blower","text":"How to Connect an External Blower"},{"level":2,"id":"h-1-preparation","text":"1. Preparation"},{"level":3,"id":"h-1-consumable-preparation","text":"① Consumable preparation"},{"level":3,"id":"h-2-debug-software","text":"② Debug software"},{"level":2,"id":"h-2-operation-step","text":"2. Operation step"}],"technical_version":"unknown"}